**Create the DLQ first, then main queue with redrive policy.**

Terraform example:

```hcl
resource "aws_sqs_queue" "main_dlq" {
  name                      = "order-processing-dlq"
  message_retention_seconds = 1209600  # 14 days max
}

resource "aws_sqs_queue" "main" {
  name                       = "order-processing"
  visibility_timeout_seconds = 60  # >= max processing time
  message_retention_seconds  = 345600  # 4 days

  redrive_policy = jsonencode({
    deadLetterTargetArn = aws_sqs_queue.main_dlq.arn
    maxReceiveCount     = 3
  })
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "dlq_depth" {
  alarm_name          = "order-dlq-has-messages"
  comparison_operator = "GreaterThanThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 1
  metric_name         = "ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible"
  namespace           = "AWS/SQS"
  period              = 300
  statistic           = "Maximum"
  threshold           = 0
  dimensions = {
    QueueName = aws_sqs_queue.main_dlq.name
  }
}
```

**Consumer code (Spring Boot with Spring Cloud AWS)**:

```java
@Component
public class OrderProcessor {
    @SqsListener("order-processing")
    public void process(Order order, @Header("ApproximateReceiveCount") int receiveCount) {
        try {
            log.info("Processing order {} (attempt {})", order.getId(), receiveCount);
            orderService.fulfill(order);
        } catch (TransientException e) {
            log.warn("Transient failure for order {}, will retry", order.getId(), e);
            throw e;  // triggers SQS retry via visibility timeout
        } catch (PoisonMessageException e) {
            log.error("Poison message, sending to DLQ immediately", e);
            // throw RuntimeException() to let SQS send to DLQ after maxReceiveCount
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```

**Use SQS redrive to reprocess DLQ messages after fix:**

```bash
# Via AWS console: DLQ → Start DLQ redrive
# Or via API:
aws sqs start-message-move-task \
  --source-arn arn:aws:sqs:us-east-1:123:order-processing-dlq \
  --destination-arn arn:aws:sqs:us-east-1:123:order-processing \
  --max-number-of-messages-per-second 10
```

**Handle partial batch failure in Lambda.** When Lambda is the consumer, it receives a batch. If one message fails but you return success, ALL messages are marked processed (losing the failed one). Use `ReportBatchItemFailures`:

```java
public SQSBatchResponse handleRequest(SQSEvent event, Context context) {
    List<SQSBatchResponse.BatchItemFailure> failures = new ArrayList<>();
    for (SQSEvent.SQSMessage msg : event.getRecords()) {
        try {
            process(msg);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            failures.add(SQSBatchResponse.BatchItemFailure.builder()
                .withItemIdentifier(msg.getMessageId()).build());
        }
    }
    return SQSBatchResponse.builder().withBatchItemFailures(failures).build();
}
```

Only failed message IDs are retained in the queue; successful ones deleted.
